<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame illuminated">
    <p class="kicker">Prime–zero intertwiner audit</p>
    <h2 id="t-rh-audit-prime-zero-intertwiner">A canonical positive feature map does not prove its global frame bound</h2>
    <p>For \(\rho=1/2+\eta+i\gamma\), Stage 40 defines</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
      \psi_{\eta,\gamma}(n)=
      \frac{\sqrt{\Lambda(n)}n^{-1-\eta-i\gamma}}
      {\sqrt{-\zeta'(2+2\eta)/\zeta(2+2\eta)}}.
    \]</p>
    <p>Its norm is one and its diagonal is exactly \(p_\eta\), independent of \(\gamma\). With positive
      convergent reflected-zero weights, the global diagonal \(P_\xi\) therefore satisfies</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
      \mathrm{RH}\iff P_\xi=p_0
      \iff \sup_{p^k}\frac{P_\xi(p^k)}{p_0(p^k)}&lt;\infty.
    \]</p>
    <p>This is an equivalence, not a proof of the required bound. Any off-line component has a positive tail
      growing as \(n^{2|\eta|}\), so it cannot cancel. Direct averaging of the feature vector retains or deletes
      the ordinate mode. The original audit then overstated the role of the coherent quadratic off-diagonals:
      they exist, but they need not be estimated merely to extract the diagonal.</p>
    <p><strong>Verdict:</strong> exact feature construction and RH-equivalent boundedness criterion proved;
      arithmetic frame identity unproved. RH remains open. <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <p class="kicker">Logarithmic-dephasing correction</p>
    <h2 id="t-rh-audit-logarithmic-dephasing">Lift first, then average the density operator</h2>
    <p>Put \(U_te_n=e^{-it\log n}e_n\) and define</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
      \mathcal D_T(A)=\frac1{2T}\int_{-T}^{T}U_tAU_t^*dt.
    \]</p>
    <p>The \((n,m)\) entry acquires the multiplier \(\operatorname{sinc}(T\log(n/m))\). It converges to zero
      for \(n\ne m\) and remains one for \(n=m\). The trace-norm limit is therefore the completely positive,
      trace-preserving diagonal pinching map, and</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
      \mathcal D(|\psi_{\eta,\gamma}\rangle\langle\psi_{\eta,\gamma}|)
      =\operatorname{diag}(p_\eta).
    \]</p>
    <p>This resolves phase removal and off-diagonal elimination without Weil positivity or critical Chebyshev
      energy. The diagonal retains \(\eta\), recoverable from two likelihood ratios; \(\gamma\) and multiplicity
      can remain in a classical register.</p>
    <p>The correction does not prove centrality. The twirl is spectral postprocessing, not a fixed-prime
      identity. Showing \(P_\xi=p_0\), or only \(P_\xi\le Cp_0\), is still equivalent to RH.</p>
    <p><strong>Verdict:</strong> pair control is unnecessary for constructing the dephased positive map. The
      global arithmetic frame bound remains unproved, and RH remains open. <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame illuminated">
    <p class="kicker">Mellin-ladder audit</p>
    <h2 id="t-rh-audit-dephased-mellin-ladder">A weaker countable target still begins with an open zero-free strip</h2>
    <p>Uniform domination can be replaced by</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
      A_j=\sum_{n=p^k}P_\xi(n)n^{1-1/j}&lt;\infty
      \qquad(j=1,2,\ldots).
    \]</p>
    <p>An off-line component at displacement \(\eta\) makes the \(j\)-th sum diverge once
      \(2|\eta|\ge1/j\). Thus all rungs are finite exactly under RH. The trace-one identity proves only
      \(A_1=1\). The next rung \(A_2&lt;\infty\) already excludes every zero outside
      \(1/4&lt;\Re\rho&lt;3/4\), a theorem not supplied by the framework.</p>
    <p>The same boundary appears through relative moments: \(P_\xi/p_0\in L^q(p_0)\) for every finite
      \(q&gt;1\) is RH-equivalent. A reflected \(\eta=0.1\) state satisfies normalization, positivity,
      dephasing, finite entropy and componentwise dissipation while its fifth Mellin rung diverges.</p>
    <p><strong>Verdict:</strong> the \(L^\infty\) condition has been weakened to scalar positive sums, but no
      nontrivial rung has been proved for the actual divisor. RH remains open. <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <p class="kicker">Hundred-round separator audit</p>
    <h2 id="t-rh-audit-hundred-round-mellin-search">Finite structural bootstrapping cannot cross a Mellin boundary</h2>
    <p>For every finite \(J\), a displacement satisfying</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
      \frac1{2(J+1)}&lt;\eta_J&lt;\frac1{2J}
    \]</p>
    <p>produces a reflected state with finite \(A_1,\ldots,A_J\) and divergent \(A_{J+1}\). It also retains all
      ten mechanisms tested across the one hundred routes: positivity, normalization, reflection, dephasing,
      finite entropy, fixed log moments, Fisher flow, unit phases, trace class and strict convexity.</p>
    <p>The countermodel is abstract and does not replace the actual zeta divisor. Its role is precise: it proves
      that finite recombinations of the established structural facts cannot imply the next moment. A successful
      continuation must add a new arithmetic identity special to \(\xi\).</p>
    <p><strong>Verdict:</strong> one hundred routes completed; zero closures. A general finite-bootstrap no-go
      is proved for the tested class, but no new zero-free strip or RH proof follows. <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></p>
  </div>
</section>

